        "created_at": 1794506615.5272818
      },
      "rev_n_1_a85ae4_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_a85ae4_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_a85ae4",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the GCD of all numbers in each pair and find the smallest prime factor of these GCDs. If the smallest prime factors are the same for all pairs, then that prime factor is the WCD. Otherwise, there is no WCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_a85ae4_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ece55f6584",
        "created_at": 1794506626.9056304
      },
      "rev_n_2_cc74a6_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_cc74a6_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_cc74a6",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through potential divisors starting from 2 up to the maximum value in the pairs and check if they divide at least one element in each pair. This approach ensures that we consider larger possible divisors more quickly, potentially reducing the overall time complexity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_cc74a6_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_264fc4b778",
        "created_at": 1794506645.1830518
      },
      "rev_n_3_5d224d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_5d224d_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_5d224d",
        "thought_text": "To address the issue, we need to ensure that the algorithm correctly identifies the WCD by checking all elements in each pair, not just the minimum values. We should iterate through all pairs and find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of each pair, then find the GCD of these GCDs to get the WCD. This approach ensures that we consider all elements in the pairs and correctly determine the WCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_5d224d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e62fa9e798",
        "created_at": 1794506688.7641847
      },
      "rev_n_4_0b0a5e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_0b0a5e_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_0b0a5e",
        "thought_text": "Check if all GCDs have a common prime factor.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8742386506143672870",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506709.760885
      },
      "rev_n_5_937d92_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_937d92_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_937d92",
        "thought_text": "Use a sieve-like approach to identify the smallest common factor among all GCDs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8742386506143672870",
